<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! \tick

Device lifecycle hook: run this block once per //nalu// (simulation tick / refresh wave).
Verse equivalent: `OnSimulate(StagedUpdates)<suspends>` entry point.

''Standing:'' the grammar table registers `\tick` (`packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-ast/grammar-table.generated.ts`, derived from the sigil tiddlers); no runtime executes it. It carries
no full pono law spec and no Hawaiian proper name: both wake on the shape of Visual Verse's tick node.
The //nalu// (wave) names the infrastructure concept below this; `\tick` serves as the grammar-layer
hook into the nalu. See [[nalu|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/nalu]] for the wave architecture.

The concurrency runtime stands before it on the founding road in the kahu workbench; the record keeps the hook's earlier
status lines (<<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/concurrency-sigils-record`>>).

<<~/ahu>>

